/// The Phase 1 inspection report for one scan (task B9), written by the pipeline (B10) and
/// the report builder (B11). Code picks the verdict from a truth table; Claude writes
/// `summary.text` from words only (S5). Every stored finding of the scan appears exactly
/// once: in `findings` (a model judged its state), `not_inspected` (nobody looked at it, I3)
/// or `insufficient_evidence` (looked at, could not be judged, with the reason, I4). No
/// probability number appears anywhere: confidence is a word (I6). A vision finding is a
/// suspect; only a meter reading proves or rules out (I1, I2).
///
/// A row judged by the design engine, or a summary it wrote, names the design it was judged
/// against.
// MARK: - Report
public struct Report: Codable, Sendable {
    /// Findings from a flipped (object-moved) segment, the mini-scan of the bottom, that the
    /// backend could not line up with the main scan: they are real findings, listed in their
    /// buckets as usual, but have no 3D point on the model. Each comes with its crop so the app
    /// can show it as a photo. Absent when every such segment was aligned or the scan has none.
    /// Why a segment was not aligned: capture.segments[].why_not.
    public let bottomNotPlaced: [BottomNotPlacedOnTheModel]?
    /// Unique per report build (report.publish); a later revision of the same build (the fix,
    /// the mesh) keeps it. A patch applies only while the row still carries its build's id
    /// (created_at has whole seconds).
    public let buildID: String?
    public let capture: Capture
    /// Issues the vision model judged cosmetic (looks worn but would not stop the device
    /// working). Listed apart; they never make the verdict potential_issues on their own.
    public let cosmetic: [CosmeticElement]?
    public let createdAt: Date
    /// Present when the design engine judged this scan against the product's own design;
    /// required when a row names `grain` or the summary says it is not words only. `project` is
    /// the design the scan was judged against.
    public let design: Design?
    /// Regions a model judged: an issue, or `none` (looked at, no visible issue). Ranked in
    /// code, most likely problem first (repairos.report.build.rank_key); cosmetic issues are in
    /// `cosmetic`.
    public let findings: [CosmeticElement]
    /// Optional "Fix it": where to buy the part of the top finding, from a public shopping
    /// search (repairos.references.parts). Only title, displayed price, seller and link are
    /// kept; no page, text or image. Added when the search is ready; never evidence and never
    /// delays the report.
    public let fix: FixClass?
    /// Regions looked at that could not be judged (I4), each with the reason.
    public let insufficientEvidence: [InsufficientEvidenceElement]
    /// What photos cannot tell (always shown), plus a meter suggestion when a reported symptom
    /// is not explained.
    public let limits: [String]?
    /// The scan's 3D mesh for the 3D view: LiDAR TSDF, decimated, vertex-coloured, in the frame
    /// of every finding's location (pins sit on it as they are).
    public let mesh: Mesh?
    /// Provenance: which model (and version) did each step, or why a step did not run.
    public let models: Models
    /// The finding_ids of the top rows of `findings` with an issue (at most three), ranked in
    /// code: safety > functional, then issues Jev judges as explaining the symptom, then
    /// confidence, then how many photos show it (repairos.report.build.rank_key). The app and
    /// exports lead with these.
    public let mostLikely: [String]?
    /// The one next action code chose from Jev's judgments (repairos.fusion), when there is one.
    public let nextStep: NextStep?
    /// Regions nobody looked at (I3), each with the reason. Never shown as ok.
    public let notInspected: [NotInspectedElement]
    /// What the object is, from the first photos (one vision-model call; a label photo is read).
    /// Brand and model only as printed or recognised beyond doubt, else absent.
    public let object: Object?
    /// Optional: where to look first, from public references about the identified product (web
    /// search titles and descriptions only; no third-party image or page is kept). Never
    /// evidence: a hint never makes a finding.
    public let referenceHints: ReferenceHints?
    public let reportID: String
    /// Safety notes chosen by code from the findings (repairos.report.safety); shown before
    /// anything else.
    public let safety: [Safety]?
    public let scanID: String
    public let sessionID: String
    /// Setup and assembly states (category setup: a battery missing, a cable unplugged, a cover
    /// not clipped), each with its plain fix. Not a broken part: listed apart and they never
    /// make the verdict potential_issues on their own. A setup state that is a hazard (severity
    /// safety: a battery in backwards, a loose mains wire) stays in `findings`.
    public let setup: [CosmeticElement]?
    public let summary: Summary
    /// Optional: what the person said they suspected and what the photos showed about it
    /// (repairos.references.leads.user_lead). The guess is a lead, never evidence: it only
    /// ordered the inspection; this section cites findings and never adds or changes one.
    public let userLead: UserLead?
    /// Picked in code (repairos.report.verdict truth table), never by a model. no_problems_seen
    /// (V8): nothing judged shows an issue and the capture covered the object well
    /// (config/verdict.yaml), but some regions were not checked: they are listed in
    /// verdict_reason.caveat.
    public let verdict: ReportVerdict
    public let verdictReason: VerdictReason

    public enum CodingKeys: String, CodingKey {
        case bottomNotPlaced = "bottom_not_placed"
        case buildID = "build_id"
        case capture = "capture"
        case cosmetic = "cosmetic"
        case createdAt = "created_at"
        case design = "design"
        case findings = "findings"
        case fix = "fix"
        case insufficientEvidence = "insufficient_evidence"
        case limits = "limits"
        case mesh = "mesh"
        case models = "models"
        case mostLikely = "most_likely"
        case nextStep = "next_step"
        case notInspected = "not_inspected"
        case object = "object"
        case referenceHints = "reference_hints"
        case reportID = "report_id"
        case safety = "safety"
